Thanks for the PR, Tac! I pushed a few changes:

- I rebased it on 3.x and squashed it into one commit.
- The bridge now requires `symfony/ux-image` `^3.7`, because ux-image 3.6.0 does not register the `imagor` bridge.
- The CHANGELOG entry moved to 3.7.0.
- To match the IPX bridge, the DSN option `scheme=http` is now `secure=false`.
- The port now comes from `Dsn::getPort()`.
- Validation now lives only in the factory. The provider no longer re-checks operation names and formats, because `ImageUrlGenerator` already does it.

I also changed one behavior: when `origin` is set, an absolute `src` no longer bypasses it.

Before, the app signed a URL to any host whenever `src` came from user data, such as an avatar URL. That meant the signature no longer protected the Imagor server.

Without `origin`, absolute URLs still pass through to the server as before.
